              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nREFDIS\n\nU.S. District Court\nCalifornia Northern District (Oakland)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 4:21-cr-00052-YGR All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. Darabi, et al. Date Filed: 02/09/2021\n\nOther court case number: 6:21-mj-00033-KK-1 Western District of Louisiana (Lafayette)\n\nAssigned to: Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers\nReferred to: Magistrate Judge Kandis A. Westmore\n\nDefendant (1)\nPooya Darabi represented by John Timothy Philipsborn\nAttorney at Law\n507 Polk Street, Suite 350\nSan Francisco, CA 94102\n(415) 771-3801\nEmail: JPhilipsbo@aol.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nElizabeth Kelley\nElizabeth Kelley, LPA, Inc.\n2525 E 29th Ave\nSuite 10-B # 225\nSpokane, WA 99223\n509-991-7058\nEmail: zealousadvocacy@aol.com\nPRO HAC VICE\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nGraham E. Archer\nFederal Public Defender\n13th Floor Federal Building - Suite 1350N\n1301 Clay Street\nOakland, CA 94612\n(510) 637-3500\nFax: (510) 637-3507\nEmail: Graham_Archer@fd.org\nTERMINATED: 02/25/2021\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender\nAppointment\n\nRandy Sue Pollock\nAttorney at Law\n286 Santa Clara Avenue\nOakland, CA 94610\n510-763-9967\nFax: 510-380-6551\nEmail: rsp@rspollocklaw.com\nTERMINATED: 11/14/2024\nDesignation: Retained\n\nSeth P. Chazin\nAttorney at Law\n1164 Solano Avenue\nAlbany, CA 94706\n510-507-8100\nFax: 510-525-0087\nEmail: sethpchazin@gmail.com\nTERMINATED: 04/12/2022\nDesignation: Retained\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:2252(a)(2) and (b): Conspiracy to Receive and Distribute\nChild Pornography\n(1)\n18:2252(a)(2) and (b): Distribution of Child Pornography\n(2)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\nNone\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nNone\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nAssigned to: Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers\nReferred to: Magistrate Judge Kandis A. Westmore\n\nDefendant (2)\nAbel Garcia-De Leon represented by Angela Milella Hansen\nTERMINATED: 08/17/2022 Federal Public Defender's Office\n1301 Clay Street\nSuite 1350N\nOakland, CA 94612\n510-637-3500\nFax: 510-637-3507\nEmail: Angela_Hansen@fd.org\nTERMINATED: 04/05/2021\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender\nAppointment\n\nCharles Jason Simpson Woodson\nLaw Offices of Charles Woodson\n484 Lake Park Avenue\n# 25\nOakland, CA 94610\n510-302-8780\nEmail: cwoodson@cjswlaw.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:2252(a)(2) and (b): Conspiracy to Receive and Distribute Committed to the custody of the BOP for a term of 120 months;\nChild Pornography supervised release 10 years; $100 special assessment;\n(1) $50,000.00 restitution\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\nTerminated Counts Disposition\n18:2252(a)(2) and (b): Distribution of Child Pornography\nDismissed on government's motion\n(3)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nFelony\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Alexis Jasmine James\nUnited States Attorney's Office\n450 Golden Gate Avenue\nBox 36055\nSan Francisco, CA 94102\n(415) 436-6758\nEmail: Alexis.James@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nSamantha Bennett\nFederal Trade Commission\nWestern Region San Francisco\n90 7th Street, Suite 14-300\nSan Francisco, CA 94103\n(415) 848-5188\nEmail: sbennett@ftc.gov\nTERMINATED: 07/06/2022\nDesignation: Assistant US Attorney\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n02/09/2021 1 INDICTMENT as to Pooya Darabi (1) count(s) 1, 2, Abel Garcia-De Leon (2) count(s) 1, 3. (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/9/2021)\n(Additional attachment(s) added on 2/24/2021: # 1 Criminal Cover Sheet) (jlmS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 02/09/2021)\n02/09/2021 2 Sealing Application and Sealing Order as to Pooya Darabi, Abel Garcia-De Leon. Signed by Magistrate Judge Laurel Beeler on\n02/09/21. (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/9/2021) (jlmS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 02/09/2021)\n02/19/2021 3 Rule 5(c)(3)Documents Received from the Western District of Louisiana (Lafayette) as to Abel Garcia-De Leon (jlmS, COURT STAFF)\n(Filed on 2/19/2021) (jlmS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 02/19/2021)\n02/22/2021 Set Hearing as to Defendant Pooya Darabi\n\nArraignment / Initial Appearance set for 2/23/2021 01:00 PM in San Jose, - Videoconference Only before Magistrate Judge Virginia K.\nDeMarchi. (pmcS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/22/2021) (Entered: 02/22/2021)\n02/23/2021 5 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Virginia K. DeMarchi: Initial Appearance as to Pooya Darabi held on\n2/23/2021.\n\nThe Court directs entry of the following Order: Pursuant to the Due Process Protection Act, the Court advised government counsel of the\ngovernment's disclosure obligations under Brady v. Maryland and its progeny, and that the failure to do so in a timely manner may result\nin dismissal of the indictment or information, dismissal of individual charges, exclusion of government evidence or witnesses, or any other\nremedy that is just under the circumstances.\n\nNOT GUILTY Plea entered by Pooya Darabi (1) as to Count(s): 1 and 2. Detention Hearing set for 2/24/2021 at 01:00 PM before\nMagistrate Judge Virginia K. DeMarchi. Defendant remanded to custody. All appearances by Zoom. Defendant consents to procced by\nZoom. DPPA advised. Motion to unseal entire case is GRANTED. (Zoom: 12:59-1:10). (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/23/2021)\n(Entered: 02/24/2021)\n02/23/2021 6 CJA 23 Financial Affidavit by Pooya Darabi (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/23/2021) (Entered: 02/24/2021)\n02/23/2021 7 NO BAIL Warrant Returned Executed on 02/22/21 as to Pooya Darabi. (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/23/2021) (Entered:\n02/24/2021)\n02/24/2021 4 ORDER DUE PROCESS PROTECTION ACT as to Pooya Darabi. Signed by Magistrate Judge Virginia K. DeMarchi on 2/23/21.\n(pmcS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/24/2021) (Entered: 02/24/2021)\n02/24/2021 Set Hearing as to Defendant Pooya Darabi Detention Hearing set for 2/25/2021 01:00 PM in San Jose, - Videoconference Only before\nMagistrate Judge Virginia K. DeMarchi. (pmcS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/24/2021) (Entered: 02/24/2021)\n02/25/2021 9 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Virginia K. DeMarchi: Detention Hearing as to Pooya Darabi held on\n2/25/2021. Defendant Ordered RELEASED. Added attorney Seth P. Chazin for Pooya Darabi. Attorney Graham E. Archer terminated in\ncase as to Pooya Darabi. Status Conference set for 3/22/2021 at 01:00 PM before Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers. All appearances by\nZoom. Defendant consents to proceed by Zoom. Federal Defender is relieved as counsel of record. Defendant and sureties consent to have\nCourt sign the Release bond on their behalf. Defendant RELEASED on $50,000.00 Appearance Bond. (Zoom: 1:25-1:54). (jlmS, COURT\nSTAFF) (Filed on 2/25/2021) (Entered: 02/25/2021)\n02/25/2021 10 ORDER Setting Conditions of Release. Appearance Bond Entered as to Pooya Darabi in amount of $50,000.00. Signed by\nMagistrate Judge Virginia K. DeMarchi on 02/25/21. (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 2/25/2021) (Entered: 02/25/2021)\n03/01/2021 11 STIPULATION WITH PROPOSED ORDER UNDER THE SPEEDY TRIAL ACT as to Pooya Darabi, filed by USA, Pooya Darabi.\n(Bennett, Samantha) (Filed on 3/1/2021) Modified on 3/2/2021 (jlmS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 03/01/2021)\n03/01/2021 12 ORDER ON STIPULATION EXCLUDING TIME UNDER THE SPEEDY TRIAL ACT granting 11 Stipulation as to Pooya\nDarabi (1) Signed by Magistrate Judge Virginia K. DeMarchi on 3/1/21. (pmcS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/01/2021)\n03/11/2021 13 Receipt via Fedwire in the amount of $50,000 from Neda Sobhiazar FBO Pooya Darabi; Date receipt issued on 03/04/2021 with Receipt #\n76082617692 (rghS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 3/11/2021) (Entered: 03/11/2021)\n03/12/2021 14 STIPULATION WITH PROPOSED PROTECTIVE ORDER as to Pooya Darabi filed by USA, Pooya Darabi (Bennett, Samantha) (Filed\non 3/12/2021) Modified on 3/15/2021 (jlmS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 03/12/2021)\n03/19/2021 15 CLERKS NOTICE SETTING ZOOM HEARING AS TO DEFENDANT POOYA DARABI for the Status Conference set for Monday\n3/22/2021 09:05 AM via Zoom webinar Videoconference before Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers.\n\nThis proceeding will be held via a Zoom webinar.\n\nWebinar Access: All counsel, members of the public, and media may access the webinar information at\nhttps://www.cand.uscourts.gov/ygr\n\nhttps://ca nd-uscourts.zoomgov.com/j/1618764848?pwd=bW03Y2NvV0YrK2FQSkxoMXRxOWprQT09\n\nWebinar ID: 161 876 4848\nPassword: 715550\n\nLocal telephone dial-in:US: +1 (669) 254-5252 or +1 (646) 828-7666\n\nGeneral Order 58. Persons granted access to court proceedings held by telephone or videoconference are reminded that photographing,\nrecording, and rebroadcasting of court proceedings, including screenshots or other visual copying of a hearing, is absolutely prohibited.\n\nZoom Guidance and Setup: https://www.cand.uscourts.gov/zoom/.\n\nStatus Conference as to Defendant Pooya Darabi is set for Monday, 3/22/2021 09:05 AM ivia Zoom webinar Videoconfere nce before\nJudge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers.\n\n(This is a text-only entry generated by the court. There is no document associated with this entry.) (fs, COURT STAFF) (Filed on\n3/19/2021) (Entered: 03/21/2021)\n03/22/2021 16 ORDER granting 14 Stipulation and Protective Order as to Pooya Darabi (1). Signed by Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers on\n3/22/2021. (fs, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/22/2021)\n03/22/2021 19 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers: Status Conference as to Pooya Darabi held via Zoom Webinar\non 3/22/2021. Status Conference set for WEDNESDAY, 7/7/2021 02:00 PM via Zoom Webinar Videoconference before Judge Yvonne\nGonzalez Rogers. Court Reporter: Pam Hebel. (fs, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 3/22/2021) (Entered: 03/25/2021)\n03/23/2021 Set/Reset Hearing as to Defendant Abel Garcia-De Leon Arraignment set for 3/24/2021 01:00 PM in San Jose, - Videoconference Only\nbefore Magistrate Judge Susan van Keulen. Initial Appearance set for 3/24/2021 01:00 PM in San Jose, - Videoconference Only before\nMagistrate Judge Susan van Keulen. (jhfS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 3/23/2021) (Entered: 03/23/2021)\n03/24/2021 17 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Susan van Keulen: Initial Appearance as to Abel Garcia-De Leon held on\n3/24/2021.\n\nThe Court directs entry of the following Order: Pursuant to the Due Process Protection Act, the Court advised government counsel of the\ngovernment's disclosure obligations under Brady v. Maryland and its progeny, and that the failure to do so in a timely manner may result\nin dismissal of the indictment or information, dismissal of individual charges, exclusion of government evidence or witnesses, or any other\nremedy that is just under the circumstances.\n\nArraignment as to Abel Garcia-De Leon (2) on Count(s): 1 and 3 held on 3/24/2021. NOT GUILTY Plea entered by Abel Garcia-De Leon\n(2) on Count(s): 1 and 3. Attorney Appointment Hearing as to Abel Garcia-De Leon held on 3/24/2021. CJA23 Submitted as to Abel\nGarcia-De Leon. Added attorney Angela Milella Hansen for Abel Garcia-De Leon. Status re Detention Hearing set for 3/30/2021 at 01:00\nPM before Magistrate Judge Susan van Keulen. Defendant remanded to custody. All parties appear via Zoom. Defendant consents to\nproceed by video appearance. DPPA advised.(Zoom: 1:10-1:17). (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 3/24/2021) (Entered: 03/24/2021)\n03/24/2021 18 CJA 23 Financial Affidavit by Abel Garcia-De Leon (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 3/24/2021) (Entered: 03/24/2021)\n03/30/2021 20 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Susan van Keulen: Status Hearing as to Abel Garcia-De Leon held on\n3/30/2021. Attorney Appointment Hearing set for 4/5/2021 at 01:00 PM before Magistrate Judge Robert M. Illman. Status re Detention set\nfor 4/5/2021 at 01:00 PM before Magistrate Judge Robert M. Illman. Defendant remanded to custody. All parties appear via Zoom.\nDefendant consents to proceed by video appearance. (Zoom: 1:00-1:03). (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 3/30/2021) (Entered:\n03/30/2021)\n03/30/2021 23 NO BAIL Warrant Returned Executed on 02/18/21 as to Abel Garcia-De Leon. (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 3/30/2021) (Entered:\n03/31/2021)\n03/31/2021 21 STIPULATION WITH PROPOSED ORDER TO MODIFY CONDITIONS OF RELEASE as to Pooya Darabi (Chazin, Seth) (Filed on\n3/31/2021) Modified on 4/1/2021 (jmlS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 03/31/2021)\n03/31/2021 22 ORDER ON STIPULATION TO MODIFY CONDITIONS OF RELEASE granting 21 Stipulation as to Pooya Darabi (1) Signed\nby Magistrate Judge Virginia K. DeMarchi on 3/31/21. (pmcS, COURT STAFF) (Entered: 03/31/2021)\n04/05/2021 24 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Robert M. Illman: Status Conference as to Abel Garcia-De Leon held on\n4/5/2021. Attorney Appointment Hearing as to Abel Garcia-De Leon held on 4/5/2021. Added attorney Charles Jason Simpson Woodson\nfor Abel Garcia-De Leon. Attorney Angela Milella Hansen terminated in case as to Abel Garcia-De Leon. Status re Detention Hearing set\nfor 4/12/2021 at 01:00 PM before Magistrate Judge Robert M. Illman. Defendant consented to appear by video. (Zoom: 1:31-1:37). (jlmS,\nCOURT STAFF) (Filed on 4/5/2021) (Entered: 04/05/2021)\n04/07/2021 25 Stipulation and Protective Order as to Abel Garcia-De Leon filed by USA and Abel Garcia-De Leon. (Bennett, Samantha) (Filed on\n4/7/2021) Modified on 4/8/2021 (jmlS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 04/07/2021)\n04/08/2021 26 STIPULATION AND PROTECTIVE ORDER as to Abel Garcia-De Leon. Signed by Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers on 4/8/2021.\n(fs, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 4/8/2021) (Entered: 04/08/2021)\n04/12/2021 27 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Robert M. Illman: Status Hearing as to Abel Garcia-De Leon held on\n4/12/2021. Detention Hearing set for 4/15/2021 at 01:00 PM before Magistrate Judge Robert M. Illman. Defendant consents to Zoom\nproceedings. Parties appeared via Zoom. (Zoom: 1:29-1:32). (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 4/12/2021) (Entered: 04/12/2021)\n04/15/2021 28 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Robert M. Illman: Detention Hearing as to Abel Garcia-De Leon held on\n4/15/2021. Status Conference set for 7/7/2021 at 02:00 PM before Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers. Defendant remanded to custody.\nHearing held via Zoom; Defendant consents to video proceedings. Defendant's mother (surety) and defendant permit court to sign bond.\nDefendant to be released 4/16/21 at 9:00 AM to reside in halfway house. (Zoom: 1:05-1:32). (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 4/15/2021)\n(Entered: 04/15/2021)\n04/15/2021 29 ORDER Setting Conditions of Release. Appearance Bond Entered as to Abel Garcia-De Leon in amount of $10,000.00. Signed by\nMagistrate Judge Robert M. Illman on 04/15/21. (jlmS, COURT STAFF) (Filed on 4/15/2021) (Entered: 04/15/2021)\n06/25/2021 30 STIPULATION WITH PROPOSED ORDER to Continue Status Conference Scheduled for July 7, 2021 to August 4, 2021 and to Exclude\nTime from July 7, 2021 to August 4, 2021, as to Abel Garcia-De Leon, filed by USA, Abel Garcia-De Leon (Woodson, Charles) (Filed on\n6/25/2021) Modified on 6/29/2021 (jlmS, COURT STAFF). Modified on 6/29/2021 (jlmS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 06/25/2021)\n06/29/2021 31 ORDER [*AS MODIFIED BY THE COURT*] TO CONTINUE STATUS CONFERENCE FOR DEFENDANT ABEL GARCIA\nDE LEON SCHEDULED FOR JULY 7, 2021 TO AUGUST 11, 2020 AND TO EXCLUDE TIME FROM JULY 7, 2021 TO\nAUGUST 11, 2021 granting 30 Stipulation as to Abel Garcia-De Leon (2). Signed by Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers on 6/29/2021.\n(fs, COURT STAFF) Modified on 6/30/2021 (jlmS, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 06/29/2021)\n06/29/2021 Set/Reset Hearing as to Defendant Abel Garcia-De Leon re 31 Order on Stipulation: Status Conference set for 7/7/2021 is CONTINUED\nto